# Stage 1 prioritization pair, run B: same arrivals and meals as run A.
# Each turn reads two lines: the Waiter's choice, then the Chef's, plus one
# extra line for each rejected command that the prompt asks again for.
# Strategy: one customer at a time. The Waiter seats the next customer only
# after the previous one has paid, so T2 is never used and the queue backs up.
# Turns 1 to 3 match run A; from turn 4 the Waiter waits instead of seating.
# Result: only C1 to C3 pay, revenue $42.00, average 65.3, DEFEAT.

# Turn 1: C1 (Salad) arrives
SEAT C1
WAIT
# Turn 2
ORDER C1
PREPARE O1
# Turn 3
SERVE O1
WAIT
# Turn 4: C2 (Burger) arrives; run A seats C2 at T2, run B keeps C2 waiting
WAIT
WAIT
# Turn 5: C1 pays
WAIT
WAIT
# Turn 6: T1 is free again
SEAT C2
WAIT
# Turn 7: C3 (Pasta) arrives and waits
ORDER C2
PREPARE O2
# Turn 8
SERVE O2
WAIT
# Turn 9
WAIT
WAIT
# Turn 10: C2 pays; C4 (Salad) arrives
WAIT
WAIT
# Turn 11: C3 is seated after four turns in the queue
SEAT C3
WAIT
# Turn 12: Pasta unit 1 of 2
ORDER C3
PREPARE O3
# Turn 13: C5 (Burger) arrives. Serving the Pasta is rejected because only one
# unit is done; the Waiter is asked again and waits. Unit 2 makes it READY.
SERVE O3
WAIT
PREPARE O3
# Turn 14
SERVE O3
WAIT
# Turn 15: C3 becomes ready to pay
WAIT
WAIT
# Turn 16: C6 (Pasta) arrives. PAY is not a command (the Cashier is automatic),
# so the Waiter is asked again and waits. C3 pays at satisfaction 44.
PAY C3
WAIT
WAIT
# Turn 17: C4 is seated after seven turns in the queue
SEAT C4
WAIT
# Turn 18: C4 orders but cannot be served before the game ends
ORDER C4
PREPARE O4
